From e3c4be0ee976cac29117990616bc6a6ee28cbab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:17:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: a0-relative constant addressing for Xenos
 vertex shaders

Xenos vertex shaders can index constants with the address register:
MOVAs sets a0 = floor(x + 0.5), and a constant operand with its
const_N_rel_abs bit (plus relative_addr for a0 rather than aL) reads
c[n + a0]. Enable indirect_const_addr for Xenos vertex shaders and
emit MOVAs + a relative read for load_uniform with a non-constant
offset, instead of the if/else tree over the whole array.

Ordering: each relative read depends on its MOVA, and each MOVA comes
after the previous relative read, so no other MOVA lands in between.
Relative reads are never co-issued (the relative bits are shared by
all constant operands of an ALU instruction, a scalar constant
included), cp_src does not fold them into users, and the scalar-mov
insertion path skips their slots. Pixel shaders keep the lowering.

The disassembler prints REL(...) on relative operands and shows MOVAs
without a destination.

piglit vp-address-01 passes on this path; dEQP 17063/17075, no
regressions.

